{"id":"word:hebrew:H4058","type":"word","title":"מָדַד","subtitle":"H4058 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, to stretch ; by implication, to measure (as if by stretching a line); figuratively, to be extended","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מָדַד (H4058) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 51 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מָדַד (mâdad) means properly, to stretch ; by implication, to measure (as if by stretching a line); figuratively, to be extended First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 17 21."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מָדַד","transliteration":"mâdad","pronunciation":"maw-dad'","strong":"H4058","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4058","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יָּ֣מָד","וַ/יָּ֜מָד","וַ/יָּ֨מָד","וַ/יָּ֤מָד","וַ/יָּ֨מָד֙"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqw3ms",23],["HVqp3ms",6],["HC/Vqq3ms",3],["HC/Vqq3cp",2],["HVNi3ms",2],["HC/Vrw3ms",1],["HC/Vpw3ms/Sp3mp",1],["HC/Vpw3ms",1],["HC/Vqw3mp",1],["HC/Vqp3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, to stretch ; by implication, to measure (as if by stretching a line); figuratively, to be extended","usage":"measure, mete, stretch self.","full":"H4058. madad מָדַד 53 verb measure (Late Hebrew id. ; Phoenician מדד ; Arabic extend, stretch , a corn-measure , etc.; Assyrian madâdu , measure ; Jewish-Aramaic noun מִידָּה measure, proportion, rule ); — Qal Perfect ׳מ ( מָדָ֑ד ) Isa 40:12 9 t. Ezekiel; suffix מְדָדוֺ Ezek 42:15 , 20 ; 1 singular וּמַדֹּתִ֫י Isa 65:7 ; וּמָֽדְדוּ consecutive Deut 21:2 ; Ezek 43:10 ; וּמַדֹּתֶם consecutive Num 35:5 ; Imperfect וַיָּ֫מָד Ruth 3:15 22t. Ezekiel; 2masculine singular תָּמוֺד Ezek 45:3 ; וַיָּמֹ֫דּוּ Exod 16:18 ; תָּמֹ֫דּוּ Ezek 47:18 ; Infinitive לָמֹד Zech 2:6 ; &#8212; measure , chiefly literal (usually followed by accusative of thing ; object omitted Exod 16:18 ; Deut 21:2 ; Ezek 40:35 , compare 47:18 (but see Co); followed by accusative of measure Ruth 3:15 ; Ezek 42:19 ; 47:3-4 , (twice in verse); 47:5 ); &#8212; 1 measure of length, distance Num 35:5 (P), Deut 21:2 (D), Ezek 40:5-6 , 8 , 20 32 t. Ezekiel 40-47 Zech 2:6 . 2 of dry measure Exod 16:18 (P), Ruth 3:15 . 3 figurative of measuring waters Isa 40:12 (of ׳י ); of requital 65:7 . Niph`al Imperfect יִמַּד Hosea 2:1 ; Jer 33:22 ; יִמַּדּוּ 31:37 ; &#8212; be measured , of sand of sea Hosea 2:1 ; Jer 33:22 ; of heavens 31:37 . Pi`el Perfect וּמִדַּדֿ consecutive Job 7:4 (compare Ges § 52 . 2. R. l); Imperfect וַיְמַדֵּד 2Sam 8:2 ; וַיְמַדְּדֵם 8:2 ; אֲמַדֵּד Psa 60:8 ; 108:8 ; &#8212; 1 extend, continue (= make extent or continuation), subject עֶרֶב Job 7:4 . 2 measure, measure off , בַחֶבֶל , of apportioning Moabites to death and life, followed by suffix 2Sam 8:2 ; also object חֲבָלִים 8:2 ; metaphor of conquest, followed by accusative, Psa 60:8 = 108:8 (|| חִלֵּק ). Po. Imperfect וַיְמֹ֫דֶד Hab 3:6 (subject God, object אֶרֶץ ), measured (namely, with eye) ᵑ9 Hi AV RV, but dubious; ᵐ5 ἐσαλεύθη , אֲזִיעַ ᵑ7 , hence shook Ew Ke Or and others (from √ [ מוֺד =] מוֺט , but read then rather וַיְמֹטֵט , although מוט not elsewhere in this conjugation; We, plausibly, וַיְמֹגֵג √ מוג , compare Nahum 1:5 ). Hithpo`el וַיִּתְמֹדֵד followed by עַלהַֿיֶ֫לֶד ; 1Kin 17:21 measured (= extended, stretched) himself upon the boy.","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 17 21","keyReferences":["1Kgs 17 21","2Sam 8 2","2Sam 8 2","Deut 21 2","Exod 16 18","Ezek 40 5","Ezek 40 6","Ezek 40 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":51,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 17 21","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּתְמֹדֵ֤ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vrw3ms"},{"reference":"2Sam 8 2","book":"2Sam","chapter":8,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יְמַדְּדֵ֤/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/